---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { components, slug, title } from '../lib/manifest';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base title="Vastu" description="A small design system of Lit web components that agents can use and test.">
  <h1>Vastu</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A small design system of web components, built with Lit. Every promise it makes, from its API and keyboard
    behaviour to its theming hooks and usage guidance, is written once in a machine-readable manifest. Docs, agent
    tools and tests are all generated from that one description.
  </p>
  <p>
    The name comes from Vastu Shastra, the ancient Indian science of space, layout and proportion. Components take their
    whole look from a <em>brand</em>: <strong>Vastu</strong>, in sandstone and indigo, is the default,
    and <strong>Lekha</strong>, in paper and teal, is the second. Every brand has light, dark and high-contrast modes. Switch
    brand and mode at the top of the page; no component changes between them.
  </p>

  <h2>Components</h2>
  <ul class="cards">
    {
      components.map((c) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`${base}components/${slug(c.tagName)}/`}>
            <strong>{title(c.tagName)}</strong>
            <code>&lt;{c.tagName}&gt;</code>
          </a>
          <p>{c.summary}</p>
          <div class="preview" set:html={c['x-examples'][0].code} />
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <p><code>npm install @firstprateek/vastu @firstprateek/vastu-tokens</code>, then import a brand stylesheet and the components you use. Each component page shows how.</p>

  <h2>For agents</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="llms.txt">llms.txt</a> and <a href="llms-full.txt">llms-full.txt</a> describe every component and token.
    <code>npx -y @firstprateek/vastu-mcp</code> is an MCP server that finds components, explains their APIs and validates
    markup, and <code>npx @firstprateek/vastu-lint</code> checks a page from the command line.
    <a href="https://github.com/firstprateek/vastu/blob/main/tests/eval/FINDINGS.md">What an agent eval found</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How it's checked</h2>
  <p>
    Every change runs contract tests generated from the manifest, behaviour tests, axe accessibility checks in every
    brand and mode, visual regression at phone and desktop widths, size budgets, and a strict Content Security Policy
    with Trusted Types, in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit. Read the
    <a href="https://github.com/firstprateek/vastu/blob/main/docs/design.md">design document</a>.
  </p>
</Base>

<script>
  import '@firstprateek/vastu/all';
</script>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .cards {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr));
  }
  .cards li {
    border: 1px solid var(--va-color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--va-radius-surface);
    padding: 16px;
  }
  .cards a {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .preview {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--va-font-family-ui);
  }
  .cards p {
    margin: 8px 0 12px;
    color: var(--va-color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
